  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental lines from the 2022 Total Governmental Funds column (p4); transfers in/out 48,205 printed in the Total column (General Fund out; Auditorium & Park 46,320 and Fire 1,885 in). Roll-forward on fund balance: 214,325 + 218,359 - 271,145 + 48,205 - 48,205 = 161,539. Cash: governmental funds cash and cash equivalents 111,700 / investments 48,159 (p3, 2022 Total), beginning from the 2021 comparative column (131,712 / 47,968). Statement capital outlay 74,058 has no printed function on its row, labelled 'Capital Outlay'. Business-type lines from the proprietary statement (p6, Total column): operating revenues 244,395 (other operating revenues 15,615 counted in charges for services on the Statement of Activities p2) + interest 1,210; expenses 217,517 + interest 22,902 = 240,419 (Statement of Activities business-type expenses, p2); bond issue costs printed '-'. 'Non-operating grants' 32,389 is printed below income before transfers (Statement of Activities: capital grants and contributions), recorded in business_type.other_financing; roll: 913,582 + 245,605 - 240,419 + 32,389 = 951,157. Proprietary cash flow statement (pp7-8) not recorded (as later years; non-GAAP). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p3, totals equal the government-wide governmental column 161,539), business-type lines from the Statement of Net Position (p1); total_* from the p1 2022 Total column. Detail: budgetary comparison schedules for General, Street, Auditorium & Park, Fire, Keno, Cemetery, Water and Sewer (pp9-16; one Original and Final budget column); rows printed '-' in the Actual column omitted. Keno schedule prints no total revenues/expenditures line. Intergovernmental detail lines kept as other state aid (no grantor/type printed); Water 'Grants' has no grantor printed. Read pages 1-16 of 16"
}
